  "slug": "decoding-mitochondrial-diverse-eukaryotes-557a",
  "summary": "Preprints propose k-mer, Gaussian and MAPQ-based fixes for isoform ambiguity, with long-read tools extending resolution to annotation and proteogenomics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is improving transcript-level quantification and isoform resolution. GaussF is alignment-free, uses GC-stratified k-mer Gaussian CDF self-benchmarking, and is compared against Kallisto and Salmon. A minimal-sharing k-mer strategy isolates transcript-specific regions to reduce mapping ambiguity. CALMeR conditions long-read MAPQ filtering on transcript context with zero-one inflated beta regression, improving spike-in transcript recovery over fixed thresholds. IG-28 identifies high-confidence isoforms from bulk and single-cell full-length cDNA and reports outperforming other tools in benchmarks. Related long-read work extends downstream: DirectClean handles ONT direct-cDNA artifacts, SQANTI-evidence annotates unannotated genomes, and LRP2 adds mass-spectrometry evidence for protein isoforms. Other items, including tWhEEL, Edi-Set-Flow and the mitochondrial RNA tool, address narrower questions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
